@jaredbroad  I do not think it is possible to make an optimization method only a function as in Python. 

Due to the nature of the solver, Alglib, QP problems don't have explicit optimization function defined. There is a default quadratic function, w'Xw, minimized and all parameters are set through auxiliary functions. Moreover, it impossible to handle global scope parameters C# as easily as in Python.

In general, user would need to implement a class with `IPortfolioOptimization` interface that perform particular optimization method, fill it with proper parameters and pass it to a portfolio construction model.
